# NEURAL PAIRING v2: the score (about 82 s).
#
# D minor, 120 bpm felt in half time (kick on 1, a fat snare+clap on 3; one
# bar = 2.0 s). Dark, cinematic, confident: deep sub, a heavy sparse 909
# blown out through its own strip compressor and bus drive into a parallel
# master compressor and tape, wide dark pads, mid/low plucks and arps.
#
# MUSIC AS STORY. The two models are two VOICES:
#   Quill  = a mid-register glass pluck (quill.patch), AEOLIAN: its colour
#            note is B-flat, the minor sixth that sighs down to A.
#   Ember  = a warm low-mid saw (ember.patch), DORIAN: its colour note is
#            B-natural, the raised sixth.
# Each also owns a pad: Quill's harmony on vellum (glassy, mid), Ember's on
# tungsten (wide, low). Before the link the voices speak separately and
# their sixths rub (B-flat against B-natural): two minds, two dialects.
# Once the link forms they HOCKET: alternating notes form one melody. The
# slow forward pass is a zig-zag climb, one note per exchange, alternating
# timbre and register; both voices land on the same D when the token pops.
# The secret is a 4-note motif (D A G B-flat: "lantern") that only Quill
# plays, and that Ember plays back exactly. The mood is a Picardy third:
# Quill's harmony turns major first, Ember's follows. The stranger answers
# the motif a tritone away. The proof and title put both voices in octaves,
# then in unison, on the theme the lantern motif grew into.
#
# Every cue is placed by section (`>NAME`), so a cue can be moved by
# editing one section line (keep fx2.song's sections identical).

bpm 120
gate 0.9
tail 2

section ASSEMBLY 0..8       # 0-4 s   assembly; the two motifs, apart
section PASS1    8..16      # 4-8 s   first forward pass (lockstep, not linked)
section SHATTER  16..20     # 8.0 s   the token shatters
section HOLD     20..24     # 10-12 s drone: "neuralese"
section BRIDGES  24..30     # 12.0 s  the drop; 8 bridges at 12.0 + 0.5k
section SLOWPASS 30..46     # 15-23 s one pass, 8 exchanges at 15.8 + 0.9k
section FAST     46..52     # 23.0 s  token pop; 23-26 fast passes
section READ     52..64     # 26-32 s one read up close
section SECRET   64..74     # 32 s lantern (Quill); 36.5 s Ember plays it back
section MOOD     74..84     # 37-42 s Picardy: Quill turns major, then Ember
section GAMES    84..108    # 42-54 s window pops every 0.6 s from 42.0
section TRAIN    108..116   # 54-58 s mechanical ostinato
section ICE      116..122   # 58.0 s  frost
section RISE     122..132   # 61-66 s riser
section DROP     132..140   # 66.0 s  drop; 66.5 real partner; 68.0 stranger
section PROOF    140..156   # 70.0 s  BIG; 73.0 / 73.8 / 74.6 window hits
section TITLE    156..164   # 78-82 s title resolve, faded by 81.9

